the best stuff I've ever written...


00:21:50.862 --> 00:21:53.830
...because it's got this naive idealism thing
going on...


00:21:53.997 --> 00:21:56.990
...where ours is gonna be
the greatest love stories ever told.


00:21:57.167 --> 00:21:58.828
And I'm writing it.


00:21:59.636 --> 00:22:01.729
So I'm sitting there reading these emails...


00:22:02.172 --> 00:22:04.232
...and there's some turbulence...


00:22:04.409 --> 00:22:07.935
...and I start to have
this massive panic attack.


00:22:08.111 --> 00:22:09.977
Like nothing I've ever had.


00:22:10.214 --> 00:22:13.513
And I think it's happening...


00:22:13.684 --> 00:22:18.552
...because I can not imagine ever feeling
that way about anybody else ever again.


00:22:18.722 --> 00:22:22.056
Listen, I have never, in my life,
received anything...


00:22:22.226 --> 00:22:24.489
...like the kind of letters you wrote her.


00:22:24.661 --> 00:22:26.892
Never written one, either.


00:22:27.497 --> 00:22:29.488
And you're lucky. You're lucky in a way...


00:22:29.666 --> 00:22:32.192
...that has nothing to do
with this particular girl.


00:22:32.369 --> 00:22:33.768
But you already know that.


00:22:34.771 --> 00:22:36.966
I must sound so young to you.


00:22:37.140 --> 00:22:39.700
Yeah, well, screw you, pal.


00:22:39.877 --> 00:22:42.504
Come on. I didn't mean it like that.


00:22:42.679 --> 00:22:44.443
I know what you meant.


00:22:44.615 --> 00:22:47.242
You know, I pride myself
on being this great listener...


00:22:47.417 --> 00:22:51.115
...but whenever I meet somebody new,
I find I'm doing all the talking.


00:22:51.288 --> 00:22:52.483
What is that?


00:22:53.323 --> 00:22:55.883
Maybe you're not really
such a great listener.


00:22:56.360 --> 00:22:59.659
Maybe you're not such a great listener.


00:22:59.831 --> 00:23:03.198
No. No, that's not it.
I'm a great listener.


00:23:04.434 --> 00:23:07.232
Yeah, but that's the thing.
I hear myself talking about it.


00:23:07.404 --> 00:23:09.964
Nelson's career. Lucy's painting.


00:23:10.140 --> 00:23:13.906
Like they're my own interests and
my own accomplishments, but they're not.


00:23:14.344 --> 00:23:18.804
And I find myself wondering,
"Where am I? What am I?"


00:23:18.982 --> 00:23:20.575
Let me ask you this.


00:23:20.751 --> 00:23:23.810
Like, what is it exactly you do
with your days?


00:23:24.588 --> 00:23:26.579
You see, now, that is just so predictable.


00:23:26.757 --> 00:23:30.556
There is the perception that because
I don't have a job or I'm not in school...


00:23:30.727 --> 00:23:33.719
...that I'm sitting around doing nothing,
which is ridiculous.


00:23:33.897 --> 00:23:37.129
Most days I don't have
five seconds to myself.


00:23:37.935 --> 00:23:41.598
I'm driving somebody around or dealing
with the house or making the meals.


00:23:41.772 --> 00:23:44.365
Not to mention I'm on, like, 15 boards.


00:23:44.541 --> 00:23:46.304
I'm sorry. I didn't think that... .


00:23:46.476 --> 00:23:50.276
Yeah, I know you didn't,
but my family does, you know?


00:23:50.447 --> 00:23:54.349
I can feel them all just silently judging.
Especially Lucy.


00:23:54.518 --> 00:23:56.349
No matter what I do, l-


00:23:56.520 --> 00:23:59.786
It's like I'm just disappointing to her.


00:23:59.957 --> 00:24:02.790
Well, she's a teenager.
You're her mother.


00:24:02.960 --> 00:24:05.793
I mean, it'd be weird
if she didn't feel that way, right?


00:24:06.530 --> 00:24:11.332
I don't know. I'm sorry,
I do think about it and so I'm touchy.


00:24:11.869 --> 00:24:13.530
But maybe I could be doing more.


00:24:13.704 --> 00:24:16.297
God, I just don't wanna
look back on my life...


00:24:18.375 --> 00:24:21.572
...and wonder what part of it
belonged to me.


00:24:22.246 --> 00:24:23.940
Okay.


00:24:24.114 --> 00:24:25.308
- Yeah.
- So--


00:24:25.482 --> 00:24:27.382
That was really nice. Thank you.


00:24:27.551 --> 00:24:32.887
Yeah, you're welcome. I mean,
it was really great to talk to you.


00:24:33.056 --> 00:24:35.490
- Yeah, all right.
- Okay.


00:24:36.894 --> 00:24:39.088
- Shit.
- What?


00:24:39.263 --> 00:24:41.355
- Shit.
- What?


00:24:42.999 --> 00:24:45.195
I'm a last-word freak.


00:24:46.002 --> 00:24:47.333
- Yeah?
- Yeah.


00:24:47.504 --> 00:24:50.201
Okay, well, I'm gonna go inside.


00:24:50.373 --> 00:24:52.705
You just shout something to me
as I'm walking away.


00:24:52.876 --> 00:24:54.105
- That'd be great.
- Perfect.


00:24:54.278 --> 00:24:56.109
- Great.
- Okay.


00:24:59.883 --> 00:25:01.578
You're gonna be all right.


00:25:08.926 --> 00:25:12.190
I don't know. Do you maybe wanna
do this again? Like tomorrow or... .


00:25:13.564 --> 00:25:16.964
Oh, l-- Sorry, I can't tomorrow.
I have an appointment.


00:25:17.133 --> 00:25:19.033
Okay. All right.
Don't worry about it.


00:25:19.203 --> 00:25:22.262
- Wednesday?
- Yeah. That would be awesome.


00:25:22.439 --> 00:25:23.770
I'll come by.


00:25:23.940 --> 00:25:25.464
- Okay. Well, I guess--
- Carter.


00:25:38.688 --> 00:25:41.919
"Awesome"? That's... .


00:25:42.259 --> 00:25:45.252
Mom, I can't talk about this anymore.
It's too retarded.


00:25:45.428 --> 00:25:47.919
And I really do not wanna fight
with you right now.


00:25:48.098 --> 00:25:50.999
It's not a fight. It's not a fight.
It's not even a big deal.


00:25:51.167 --> 00:25:53.727
I'm just saying
he's basically alone over there.


00:25:53.903 --> 00:25:55.632
You could just take him to a movie.


00:25:55.805 --> 00:25:58.672
Do you have any idea
how lame that would sound?


00:25:59.542 --> 00:26:03.842
It would redefine lame. Seriously.
Are you ready to make history?


00:26:06.816 --> 00:26:08.511
She might have a point, sweetheart.


00:26:08.685 --> 00:26:11.518
It could be a little awkward.
What do we know about this guy?


00:26:11.688 --> 00:26:14.054
Forget it. Just forget it.


00:26:14.224 --> 00:26:17.660
I thought maybe, maybe, just do
something nice for somebody sometime...


00:26:17.827 --> 00:26:20.489
...but I can't handle the two of you
ganging up on me.


00:27:14.217 --> 00:27:16.549
This is happening
because we're all really scared.


00:27:16.720 --> 00:27:19.746
So I'm gonna say to you
the same thing I said to her.


00:27:19.923 --> 00:27:23.290
Whatever we find out tomorrow,
we deal with it together.


00:27:24.094 --> 00:27:26.289
Now, your daughter
would like to apologize...


00:27:26.463 --> 00:27:28.692
...and she said, if you really want her to...


00:27:28.864 --> 00:27:32.425
...she'll go across the street now
and ask Crazy's grandson out on a date.


00:27:32.602 --> 00:27:35.070
He's a sweet kid. I feel bad for him.


00:27:35.238 --> 00:27:38.331
He's heartsick.


00:27:42.645 --> 00:27:45.273
I'm gonna be with you every second.


00:28:04.600 --> 00:28:06.125
What?


00:28:07.137 --> 00:28:08.364
Well, I'm just curious.


00:28:08.537 --> 00:28:12.770
Do you ever worry that you're gonna
get stuck in one of those positions?


00:28:14.443 --> 00:28:17.105
Yes, I do.


00:28:18.481 --> 00:28:19.971
Ready for bed?


00:28:21.217 --> 00:28:23.879
Did you know yoga increases circulation...


00:28:24.053 --> 00:28:27.784
...promotes health and well-being
and also reduces anxiety?


00:28:27.957 --> 00:28:29.925
Yeah, I've read that.


00:28:30.459 --> 00:28:32.893
Well, maybe you could try it.


00:28:37.099 --> 00:28:39.967
Hey, you know what?


00:28:42.038 --> 00:28:47.237
I'm sorry if I've seemed
a little bit distracted lately.


00:28:48.678 --> 00:28:50.235
It's cool.


00:28:59.722 --> 00:29:01.383
Good night, muffin.


00:29:02.825 --> 00:29:04.656
Did you get my pills?


00:29:04.827 --> 00:29:08.093
Yeah, these are some pretty serious
tranquilizers you got here.


00:29:08.264 --> 00:29:11.858
Are you sure it's safe
to be taking these all at once?


00:29:16.872 --> 00:29:18.499
I love it.


00:29:27.450 --> 00:29:29.475
Who changed the sheets?


00:29:29.652 --> 00:29:31.118
I did.


00:29:45.133 --> 00:29:46.725
Who's Sofia?


00:29:48.804 --> 00:29:50.204
How did you know about that?


00:29:50.373 --> 00:29:53.466
Oh, you kind of mutter in your sleep.


00:29:53.643 --> 00:29:55.577
What are you doing in my room
when I'm sleeping?


00:29:55.745 --> 00:29:58.611
That's a really good question.


00:30:02.852 --> 00:30:04.978
Well, she was my girlfriend...


00:30:05.153 --> 00:30:07.679
...and she doesn't wanna
be with me anymore.


00:30:08.156 --> 00:30:09.817
Is she zaftig?


00:30:11.360 --> 00:30:13.794
Yeah. Spectacular, actually.


00:30:13.962 --> 00:30:16.487
That's so important.


00:30:55.771 --> 00:30:57.500
I'm Sofia.


00:31:00.443 --> 00:31:03.536
<i>I am completely in love with you.</i>


00:31:12.120 --> 00:31:13.382
Goodbye.


00:31:33.009 --> 00:31:34.670
Hey. How you doing?


00:31:38.347 --> 00:31:40.407
- Yes?
- Do you know where you are?


00:31:40.582 --> 00:31:43.142
I'm just regrouping.


00:31:47.422 --> 00:31:51.119
- I could give you a ride home if you want.
- No. I'm good.


00:31:51.294 --> 00:31:54.262
Gotta keep running. It's healthy.


00:32:15.484 --> 00:32:17.145
Actually, you know what?


00:32:19.488 --> 00:32:23.618
My mom and I kind of
got into this fight the other night.


00:32:23.792 --> 00:32:26.625
I mean, it wasn't really a fight,
it was just... .


00:32:26.795 --> 00:32:30.287
She wanted me to maybe ask you
if you wanted...


00:32:31.133 --> 00:32:32.725
...to go see a movie or something.


00:32:34.369 --> 00:32:36.894
And I told her
that it would be really embarrassing.


00:32:37.072 --> 00:32:39.472
It would be the last thing
that you'd want to do.


00:32:39.641 --> 00:32:44.271
I mean, some creepy girl accosting you
like you're some kind of charity.


00:32:44.713 --> 00:32:46.203
This is really coming out wrong.


00:32:46.381 --> 00:32:50.750
Your parents, they normally pretty cool
about letting you go out on a school night?


00:32:50.919 --> 00:32:52.045
Not really.


00:32:52.220 --> 00:32:55.519
Do you think if you were
taking me to a movie...


00:32:55.691 --> 00:32:58.182
...being neighborly,
they might make an exception?


00:32:59.561 --> 00:33:00.585
I don't know.


00:33:00.762 --> 00:33:03.424
All right. Find out. Get back to me.


00:33:13.541 --> 00:33:14.907
What is it?


00:33:15.210 --> 00:33:17.337
It's possible...


00:33:17.512 --> 00:33:20.276
...I think maybe...


00:33:20.949 --> 00:33:23.440
...my toilet might be stopped up.


00:33:23.618 --> 00:33:26.519
Maybe? What's the variable?


00:33:26.688 --> 00:33:29.679
Water's running over the top.


00:33:29.858 --> 00:33:31.849
The carpet's all wet.


00:33:32.794 --> 00:33:37.094
Well, I'll take a look. First, I just gotta
stop off in my room and kill myself.


00:33:54.082 --> 00:33:56.550
I think I should tell Paige alone.


00:33:56.718 --> 00:33:59.482
I think it's less scary
if it's coming from me...


00:33:59.654 --> 00:34:01.587
...and she sees that I'm fine.


00:34:02.057 --> 00:34:03.285
I think you're right.


00:34:04.392 --> 00:34:05.723
But I want you to tell Lucy.


00:34:11.600 --> 00:34:13.157
It's better that way.


00:34:13.735 --> 00:34:17.261
So he goes, "Find out. Get back to me."


00:34:17.439 --> 00:34:19.872
Which is not exactly like, whatever...


00:34:20.041 --> 00:34:22.873
...but it definitely indicates
that he might be, you know--


00:34:23.044 --> 00:34:25.740
- Interested?
- Yeah. Kind of, right?


00:34:25.914 --> 00:34:29.475
I mean, even if he were,
it would still be the most awkward--


00:34:29.651 --> 00:34:31.710
- Do it.
- You think?


00:34:31.886 --> 00:34:34.321
Yeah. You have to do it.
And you know what else?


00:34:34.489 --> 00:34:38.152
Like, seriously,
you have to take me with you.


00:34:46.401 --> 00:34:49.267
All right. Somebody better tell me
what's going on here.


00:34:50.905 --> 00:34:53.898
I really want ice cream.
I've been thinking about that all day.


00:34:54.074 --> 00:34:55.406
Who wants to come with me?


00:34:55.577 --> 00:34:57.841
Wait, but what--?


00:34:58.013 --> 00:34:59.708
You want me to go get ice cream?


00:35:02.082 --> 00:35:04.744
You know what? You two go ahead.


00:35:05.387 --> 00:35:08.982
Lucy and I are gonna take Bozo for a walk.
Come on. It'll be good.


00:35:18.365 --> 00:35:20.061
Does it hurt?


00:35:23.705 --> 00:35:25.070
No.


00:35:28.209 --> 00:35:32.271
The chemotherapy can be rough,
and they said there's nausea.


00:35:33.949 --> 00:35:36.008
And it could make me tired.


00:35:38.954 --> 00:35:40.785
Are you scared?


00:35:42.122 --> 00:35:44.216
Yeah, sometimes.


00:35:44.893 --> 00:35:48.795
Not right now, though.
Right now I feel pretty tough.


00:35:51.333 --> 00:35:53.300
You don't look so tough.


00:35:59.274 --> 00:36:01.105
I took $20 from your purse.


00:36:02.576 --> 00:36:04.101
Really? When?


00:36:04.980 --> 00:36:08.507
A while ago. Last February.


00:36:09.618 --> 00:36:10.982
Are you serious?


00:36:11.485 --> 00:36:12.919
Yeah.


00:36:14.521 --> 00:36:17.286
I've been wanting to tell you for a while.


00:36:17.759 --> 00:36:20.420
I felt bad about it. I'm sorry.


00:36:20.594 --> 00:36:24.360
Well, just out of curiosity,
what did you need $20 for?


00:36:25.000 --> 00:36:26.763
It's stupid.


00:36:27.334 --> 00:36:31.828
I wanted to start saving money,
you know, for the future.


00:36:33.807 --> 00:36:36.208
But I didn't have any money...


00:36:37.112 --> 00:36:39.046
...so I needed a foundation.


00:36:40.347 --> 00:36:43.340
Right. Well, at least
you're financially responsible.


00:36:45.886 --> 00:36:49.880
I'm telling you because other than that,
I don't have any secrets from you.


00:36:50.057 --> 00:36:53.458
- It's okay to keep some things to yourself.
- Yeah, but I don't.


00:36:53.627 --> 00:36:58.088
Like, I always tell you the truth
because you always tell me the truth.


00:36:58.265 --> 00:36:59.597
Right?


00:37:01.635 --> 00:37:03.296
Right.


00:37:03.704 --> 00:37:07.037
If you say everything's gonna be okay,
I believe you.


00:37:07.207 --> 00:37:10.370
And I know you're telling the truth
because you wouldn't lie to me.


00:37:11.246 --> 00:37:13.680
Maybe to other people...


00:37:14.848 --> 00:37:18.181
...like, maybe to Lucy
or maybe to Dad...


00:37:18.352 --> 00:37:20.013
...but not to me.


00:37:24.992 --> 00:37:27.188
I just needed to know.


00:37:30.030 --> 00:37:32.157
Are you gonna be okay?


00:38:15.242 --> 00:38:16.574
Hey.


00:38:20.147 --> 00:38:22.047
What's going on?


00:38:22.449 --> 00:38:25.385
You look good.
You look better than you did the other day.


00:38:35.496 --> 00:38:38.590
- So, what was her name?
- Sorry?


00:38:38.767 --> 00:38:42.497
- The girl you wrote all those letters to.
- Oh, Sofia.


00:38:44.271 --> 00:38:47.035
- Was she your first love?
- Yeah.


00:38:47.207 --> 00:38:49.198
Well, there was somebody
in high school...


00:38:49.376 --> 00:38:52.368
...but I used to have this tendency
to project onto girls...


00:38:52.546 --> 00:38:55.414
...my fantasies of what
I thought they should be like.


00:38:55.582 --> 00:38:58.551
Didn't have anything to do
with what they were actually like.


00:38:58.719 --> 00:39:01.187
It would just take me forever
to figure that out.


00:39:01.355 --> 00:39:03.755
Usually four to five months.


00:39:04.625 --> 00:39:06.422
But Sofia was different?


00:39:06.593 --> 00:39:08.959
Yeah. Well, you know.


00:39:11.932 --> 00:39:15.265
No. Actually, that was pretty much
the same deal.


00:39:16.570 --> 00:39:18.060
Well... .


00:39:19.974 --> 00:39:22.703
Come on.
There's something I wanna show you.


00:39:27.147 --> 00:39:30.548
This is exciting.
Do you know where we're going?


00:39:30.718 --> 00:39:34.153
<i>I feel like we're gonna
run into the cast of Deliverance.</i>


00:39:35.289 --> 00:39:36.881
Love it here.


00:39:38.158 --> 00:39:41.992
I have this whole science-fiction scenario
worked out...


00:39:42.930 --> 00:39:47.128
...where I pretend that since
there's no evidence of modern life...


00:39:47.301 --> 00:39:49.462
...that I could walk out of these woods...


00:39:49.637 --> 00:39:54.130
...and be in another time
and a different place.


00:39:54.308 --> 00:39:56.208
I love that.


00:40:07.955 --> 00:40:10.584
My husband has been having an affair.


00:40:12.493 --> 00:40:16.156
I found out a while ago
and I didn't do anything about it.


00:40:19.766 --> 00:40:23.725
I told myself
it's because of the girls and... .


00:40:28.108 --> 00:40:31.600
I just have a very comfortable life.
It's very clean.


00:40:32.079 --> 00:40:33.740
I'm good at that, you know?


00:40:35.616 --> 00:40:40.019
And the thing is, he's really a decent guy.
I mean, he's a good provider and... .


00:40:41.722 --> 00:40:45.852
Anyway, it's discreet, I guess.
I don't know.


00:40:46.660 --> 00:40:48.593
That must sound pretty vacant to you.


00:40:49.696 --> 00:40:54.099
I wouldn't even begin to know
how to have an opinion about that.


00:40:57.070 --> 00:40:59.129
The thing is, I just don't... .


00:40:59.506 --> 00:41:01.440
I just don't love him.


00:41:02.042 --> 00:41:04.772
Not like you love her.
Not like that kind of love...


00:41:04.945 --> 00:41:06.810
...where it hurts when it's good...


00:41:06.979 --> 00:41:09.210
...especially when it's good, you know?


00:41:10.883 --> 00:41:14.820
The further away I get from that
and the more I talk to you, you know...


00:41:15.154 --> 00:41:17.521
...l'm not so sure
that was real love either.


00:41:22.062 --> 00:41:25.156
You know, I'd really like
just to give you a hug right now.


00:41:25.332 --> 00:41:26.993
Would that be weird?


00:41:50.991 --> 00:41:53.619
Hey, Lucy can't know anything
about Nelson's--


00:41:53.794 --> 00:41:56.354
- Sarah.
- Right.


00:41:56.729 --> 00:41:58.560
Goes without saying.


00:41:59.098 --> 00:42:03.832
You know, she asked me about taking you
to a movie on a school night specifically.


00:42:04.004 --> 00:42:06.471
We usually don't let her
go out on the weekdays.


00:42:06.673 --> 00:42:09.198
That's responsible.


00:42:09.375 --> 00:42:10.967
I'm making an exception.


00:42:11.144 --> 00:42:13.134
I'm guessing tomorrow
you probably have... .


00:42:13.312 --> 00:42:16.441
Yeah. Another appointment.


00:42:17.583 --> 00:42:21.645
Hey, look, I don't know
when I'm gonna be able to do this again.


00:42:21.822 --> 00:42:25.656
It might be a couple days, might be longer.
I do have a lot of stuff coming up.


00:42:25.826 --> 00:42:27.259
All right.


00:42:29.028 --> 00:42:31.395
- But I have to go to the grocery store.
- I'll go.


00:42:31.565 --> 00:42:33.156
- Okay.
- Great, yeah.


00:42:33.966 --> 00:42:36.299
I had never been to New York before.
I loved it.


00:42:36.470 --> 00:42:42.339
And I remember that I was sitting alone
in the American Wing of the Met.


00:42:42.508 --> 00:42:45.068
I was in the room
where they have all the paintings...


00:42:45.244 --> 00:42:47.075
...from the Hudson River Valley School.


00:42:47.246 --> 00:42:51.707
I just suddenly had this feeling
like I was awake.


00:42:51.984 --> 00:42:57.981
Finally, awake to my life. Like I was
exactly where I was suppose to be.


00:42:59.126 --> 00:43:01.321
And then the other day...


00:43:01.495 --> 00:43:05.191
