01:02:38.968 --> 01:02:42.266
And I would be indebted to you for, like...


01:02:42.437 --> 01:02:44.268
...the rest of time.


01:02:55.350 --> 01:03:00.185
This is just like a dream I have.
But I'm naked except for my sneakers.


01:03:00.790 --> 01:03:05.250
Ladies and gentlemen,
the amazingly beautiful Lucy Hardwicke.


01:03:05.428 --> 01:03:10.229
Tonight she's wearing a designer dress
and is escorted by this guy.


01:03:10.399 --> 01:03:13.459
- Hey, how's it going?
- Howard Portchnik.


01:03:14.604 --> 01:03:17.072
- What did you say your name was?
- Howard Portchnik.


01:03:17.240 --> 01:03:20.641
- Portchnik. And your father?
- Rodney Portchnik.


01:03:20.810 --> 01:03:22.607
- Is he here?
- In Bermuda, actually.


01:03:22.778 --> 01:03:25.041
I don't think I'd be having this party
if he was.


01:03:25.214 --> 01:03:27.808
- Have fun, kids, stay awesome.
- Okay.


01:03:28.985 --> 01:03:30.145
What was that?


01:03:30.319 --> 01:03:34.220
I think, like a million years ago,
my mom had a thing for that guy's dad.


01:03:34.389 --> 01:03:37.791
Oh, my God. You're here.
That's so cool of you.


01:03:39.161 --> 01:03:40.458
And you are...?


01:03:41.364 --> 01:03:45.060
I'm her best friend. Yeah.
I don't... . Do I know you?


01:03:45.234 --> 01:03:47.497
I don't know.


01:03:47.669 --> 01:03:50.764
Oh, my gosh, Madison's here.


01:03:50.939 --> 01:03:55.036
Come on, I have so much I have to tell you.
It's F-ing crazy.


01:03:55.444 --> 01:03:57.742
- Go. Go, it's all right.
- You sure?


01:03:57.914 --> 01:03:59.972
It's crazy. I'll be around.


01:04:08.558 --> 01:04:09.956
We drank so much.


01:04:10.726 --> 01:04:13.217
Whoa, hey, you're here. I mean--


01:04:13.396 --> 01:04:15.421
I'm a real party animal.


01:04:17.033 --> 01:04:20.491
- So how you doing?
- I'm good. Actually, I'm really good.


01:04:20.670 --> 01:04:22.160
Oh, that's good.


01:04:23.138 --> 01:04:28.839
If you need someone to talk to
or maybe just... .


01:04:29.011 --> 01:04:31.775
I don't know.
But I'm pretty much around anytime--


01:04:31.948 --> 01:04:34.472
Yeah, great. We gotta keep going, Lucy.


01:04:34.650 --> 01:04:38.313
There's some seniors from Carver
we want you to meet. So hot and funny.


01:04:38.754 --> 01:04:39.811
Great.


01:05:02.845 --> 01:05:05.973
This guy is a complete asshole.


01:05:07.449 --> 01:05:10.146
I could have been the son of an asshole.


01:05:14.756 --> 01:05:17.247
Mom, you're never gonna believe
where I'm standing.


01:05:17.426 --> 01:05:20.452
<i>Carter. It's Sofia.</i>


01:05:21.029 --> 01:05:23.021
<i>Are you there?</i>


01:05:23.799 --> 01:05:27.393
Yeah. Hi. Hey, how are you?


01:05:27.569 --> 01:05:30.333
<i>God, I missed you.</i>


01:05:30.706 --> 01:05:34.766
<i>So much is happening.
I don't even know where to start.</i>


01:05:34.943 --> 01:05:38.379
<i>I just feel like my whole life
is, like, crashing in.</i>


01:05:38.547 --> 01:05:39.877
<i>I cry all the time...</i>


01:05:40.048 --> 01:05:43.985
<i>... and you are the only person I can talk to
when I'm flipping out like this.</i>


01:05:44.152 --> 01:05:46.143
<i>My best friend.</i>


01:05:47.022 --> 01:05:48.683
<i>How are you?</i>


01:05:52.427 --> 01:05:53.554
<i>Carter?</i>


01:05:53.729 --> 01:05:57.596
Are you the pathetic faggot
trying to scam on Lucy?


01:05:58.767 --> 01:06:01.100
I'm gonna have to call you back.


01:06:08.210 --> 01:06:12.612
You think you can step into my 'hood,
slinging game at my girl...


01:06:12.781 --> 01:06:16.547
...drinking my boy's brew,
and expect not to be scrapping directly?


01:06:17.719 --> 01:06:20.848
- What?
- Are you deaf and stupid? I said--


01:06:21.023 --> 01:06:23.354
Don't-- Don't repeat all that, please.


01:06:23.525 --> 01:06:26.153
Okay, I think the answer
to your question...


01:06:26.327 --> 01:06:30.889
...depends on whether you have,
like, a learning disability...


01:06:31.066 --> 01:06:33.501
...or you're just an average moron.


01:06:40.742 --> 01:06:44.804
- All right.
- Okay. Above-average moron.


01:06:44.979 --> 01:06:47.140
- Don't take that.
- What was that, faggot?


01:06:51.420 --> 01:06:53.445
- Get him, Gabe.
- What the hell?


01:06:53.621 --> 01:06:56.488
- This guy is a good friend of mine.
- You complete asshole.


01:06:56.658 --> 01:06:59.491
No, you don't.
I think we all understand...


01:06:59.661 --> 01:07:02.323
...that I am not the complete asshole
in this situation.


01:07:02.497 --> 01:07:04.488
- It was your mistake.
- Would you shut--?


01:07:04.666 --> 01:07:08.102
Not me, not this guy,
whatever his name is.


01:07:08.269 --> 01:07:10.760
She's amazing.


01:07:10.939 --> 01:07:14.773
She's beautiful and intelligent
and amazing...


01:07:15.110 --> 01:07:16.271
...and you blew it.


01:07:16.945 --> 01:07:19.005
What's wrong with you?
What's wrong with me?


01:07:19.180 --> 01:07:22.172
How could I have let you drive my car?


01:07:30.692 --> 01:07:32.319
Come on.


01:07:50.279 --> 01:07:55.409
You know, that's the first time
in my entire life I've ever been punched.


01:07:55.583 --> 01:07:57.346
How was it for you?


01:07:57.752 --> 01:07:59.014
It hurt.


01:08:00.155 --> 01:08:01.588
I'm not a fan.


01:08:03.825 --> 01:08:05.884
There's something I wanna tell you.


01:08:07.662 --> 01:08:12.258
I've actually never talked about it
out loud.


01:08:12.835 --> 01:08:13.892
Okay.


01:08:14.636 --> 01:08:17.696
Something happened when I was, like, 11.


01:08:18.773 --> 01:08:20.900
I had this friend Ethan.


01:08:22.243 --> 01:08:24.541
Me and Ethan did everything together.


01:08:24.979 --> 01:08:29.643
It's not really weird to be friends
with a boy when you're 11.


01:08:29.818 --> 01:08:31.479
Anyway...


01:08:32.053 --> 01:08:34.248
...I went to his house one day.


01:08:34.656 --> 01:08:36.749
And we were just, like...


01:08:37.192 --> 01:08:39.660
...hanging out and, like, playing.


01:08:39.828 --> 01:08:44.390
Doing kid stuff. I don't know.


01:08:45.233 --> 01:08:48.031
I don't think his parents were home.


01:08:48.903 --> 01:08:52.134
It was like Truth or Dare?


01:08:52.307 --> 01:08:55.070
But, like, a game.


01:08:55.243 --> 01:08:58.609
I mean, there was clothes taken off... .


01:08:58.780 --> 01:09:02.113
I'm not really even sure, like, what--


01:09:03.484 --> 01:09:04.712
It's all right.


01:09:05.420 --> 01:09:10.153
I freaked out.
And then he freaked out.


01:09:10.325 --> 01:09:12.987
And he got really defensive, saying, like... .


01:09:13.160 --> 01:09:15.789
Like it was my fault that it went that far.


01:09:16.064 --> 01:09:18.555
The next day at school
he must have told somebody...


01:09:18.733 --> 01:09:21.224
...because it was everyone--


01:09:22.904 --> 01:09:26.135
I was just so humiliated.


01:09:27.041 --> 01:09:29.032
Teachers got involved,
and parents were--


01:09:29.210 --> 01:09:34.010
Lucy, Lucy, that kind of thing,
that happens to kids all the time.


01:09:34.181 --> 01:09:37.481
Really. It does.
It's just not that big a deal.


01:09:37.652 --> 01:09:39.677
Even though, hey,
I know it feels that way.


01:09:40.121 --> 01:09:43.113
Like, afterwards, my mom and I...


01:09:43.958 --> 01:09:46.791
...we never talked about it. At all.


01:09:48.429 --> 01:09:53.162
And I don't know, it just always
seemed like she was embarrassed.


01:09:53.334 --> 01:09:56.531
That I was, like, a pervert or something--


01:09:56.704 --> 01:09:59.035
You're not a pervert.
You didn't do anything wrong.


01:09:59.206 --> 01:10:04.167
- Then how could she let me feel that way?
- Well, you gotta stop blaming your mom.


01:10:04.745 --> 01:10:06.805
Hating her for these-- You gotta let it go.


01:10:06.981 --> 01:10:10.348
If she was not there for me
when I really needed her, why should l--?


01:10:10.518 --> 01:10:12.042
Because she might die.


01:10:16.657 --> 01:10:19.286
I'm sorry. I shouldn't have said that.


01:10:24.966 --> 01:10:26.194
What the f--?


01:10:28.603 --> 01:10:30.628
That was really hard for me to say.


01:10:30.805 --> 01:10:33.136
What, are you trying to scare me?
Congratulations.


01:10:33.307 --> 01:10:35.833
I'm trying to wake you up.


01:10:36.344 --> 01:10:40.007
There's a big fucking world out there.
It's messy and it's chaotic...


01:10:40.181 --> 01:10:42.978
...and it's never, ever,
the thing you'd expect.


01:10:43.517 --> 01:10:45.008
It is okay to be scared...


01:10:45.186 --> 01:10:48.417
...but you cannot allow your fears
to turn you into an asshole.


01:10:49.090 --> 01:10:51.581
Not when it comes to the people
that really love you.


01:10:51.759 --> 01:10:53.692
The people that need you.


01:10:58.199 --> 01:11:00.166
So I guess we're done, right?


01:11:02.003 --> 01:11:04.233
Yeah. We're done.


01:11:26.093 --> 01:11:28.186
I can't-- I don't--
I don't want to start... .


01:12:29.856 --> 01:12:33.087
Don't come any closer. Please.


01:12:34.227 --> 01:12:35.717
Okay.


01:12:36.963 --> 01:12:39.831
I just wanted to know if you're all right.


01:12:41.369 --> 01:12:43.200
Everything hurts.


01:12:52.113 --> 01:12:55.172
It's my fault. I know that.
I'm responsible.


01:12:56.817 --> 01:12:59.377
But you need to hear this, Carter.


01:13:00.555 --> 01:13:03.046
You are never gonna
touch my daughter again.


01:13:03.224 --> 01:13:06.624
- You can't see her.
- Wait, I'm sorry.


01:13:06.793 --> 01:13:08.988
- I am--
- You have to go.


01:14:56.671 --> 01:15:00.071
- What is it with you?
- I know.


01:15:00.273 --> 01:15:03.800
I mean, if you-- If you don't
want to talk to me, fine, whatever.


01:15:03.977 --> 01:15:07.640
But don't send Phyllis out to make
excuses for you, saying you're not in.


01:15:07.814 --> 01:15:11.580
Where am I suppose to believe you went?
I'm the only person you know here.


01:15:12.954 --> 01:15:16.081
- Right?
- Pretty much.


01:15:16.256 --> 01:15:19.419
It's been like a week.
I mean, five days.


01:15:20.228 --> 01:15:24.186
I don't know. I wanted to call you,
I just didn't have your cell phone number.


01:15:25.432 --> 01:15:27.957
I don't know.
I just thought that you were maybe...


01:15:28.134 --> 01:15:31.467
...like, mad at me.
- Hey, I'm not.


01:15:31.972 --> 01:15:33.803
I'm not mad at you.


01:15:34.474 --> 01:15:36.874
So you regret kissing me?


01:15:39.579 --> 01:15:43.345
Lucy, I can't. Okay?
I can't see you anymore.


01:15:51.424 --> 01:15:53.324
I just-- I wasn't the guy.


01:15:54.094 --> 01:15:58.292
Okay, then I guess-- Who is?


01:15:58.465 --> 01:16:00.558
Actually, when you think about it...


01:16:00.734 --> 01:16:03.634
...you're gonna find
that you already know.


01:16:24.190 --> 01:16:25.850
Mom.


01:16:28.962 --> 01:16:30.327
I don't feel good.


01:16:30.697 --> 01:16:32.494
I think I need--


01:16:40.907 --> 01:16:43.740
<i>- Nelson Hardwicke's office.
- Hi, this is Lucy. I need my dad.</i>


01:16:43.910 --> 01:16:48.244
<i>Lucy, he's not here. He stepped out to- -</i>


01:16:49.883 --> 01:16:52.249
Mom, we're gonna try
to stand up now. Okay?


01:16:52.419 --> 01:16:55.252
I'm gonna get you to the hospital,
but I need you to help.


01:16:55.422 --> 01:16:57.822
I can't do this by myself.
You ready?


01:17:03.196 --> 01:17:06.426
You're having what we call
a neutropenic fever.


01:17:06.598 --> 01:17:08.931
Your white-blood-cell count
dropped too low...


01:17:09.102 --> 01:17:10.933
...your body can't defend itself.


01:17:11.104 --> 01:17:13.299
I spoke with Hoffman in Ann Arbor.


01:17:13.473 --> 01:17:15.771
We're gonna put you
on a drug called Neulasta.


01:17:20.547 --> 01:17:21.605
I'm so sorry I wasn't--


01:17:21.780 --> 01:17:23.907
- What happened to her?
- You're okay.


01:17:24.084 --> 01:17:26.075
I'm gonna grab a soda.
You want anything?


01:17:26.251 --> 01:17:28.446
No. I'm good.


01:18:18.505 --> 01:18:21.440
<i>- Of course I do. You're a cad.
- I can't help it.</i>


01:18:21.608 --> 01:18:26.943
<i>- Hello?
- Hey, Sof. Sofia, it's me.</i>


01:18:27.112 --> 01:18:28.546
<i>Who?</i>


01:18:29.048 --> 01:18:30.605
Carter.


01:18:30.849 --> 01:18:35.014
<i>- Who?
- Carter Webb.</i>


01:18:35.188 --> 01:18:38.180
<i>Oh, Carter, baby.</i>


01:18:38.358 --> 01:18:42.556
<i>Hey, this is just a really bad time.</i>


01:18:42.729 --> 01:18:43.956
<i>What?</i>


01:18:44.129 --> 01:18:48.590
<i>Listen, I'm at this thing in SoHo
and everybody's wasted.</i>


01:18:48.767 --> 01:18:53.000
<i>And I'm wasted too.
It's New Year's Eve, you know?</i>


01:18:53.173 --> 01:18:55.163
No. It's not. It's October.


01:18:55.341 --> 01:18:57.809
<i>Well, it feels like New Year's Eve.</i>


01:18:57.977 --> 01:19:02.072
<i>Listen, sweetie, I really wanna
talk to you, you know?</i>


01:19:02.247 --> 01:19:06.480
<i>But let me try a little later. Okay? Okay.</i>


01:19:06.653 --> 01:19:10.453
Yeah, okay. No.
I just, you know... .


01:19:10.622 --> 01:19:12.955
I sort of... .


01:19:14.426 --> 01:19:16.190
Hello?


01:19:27.640 --> 01:19:29.767
What's wrong with you?


01:19:33.379 --> 01:19:35.812
Can't seem to get it together.


01:19:37.217 --> 01:19:39.048
I'm 26 years old.


01:19:39.219 --> 01:19:43.279
I'm healthy. I'm capable.
I've had every opportunity.


01:19:44.057 --> 01:19:46.491
My friend's are getting married
and having kids...


01:19:46.659 --> 01:19:48.957
...and I'm just so far away.


01:19:49.528 --> 01:19:51.189
Why did you come here?


01:19:51.363 --> 01:19:54.298
I'm trying to write this thing
about growing up in L.A.


01:19:54.466 --> 01:19:56.401
How long have you been trying?


01:19:57.736 --> 01:20:00.535
Oh, 11 years, give or take.


01:20:00.706 --> 01:20:03.402
Too long. You're not trying hard enough.


01:20:03.575 --> 01:20:07.602
Maybe you should think about
working on something else.


01:20:07.780 --> 01:20:09.303
Yeah. You're probably right.


01:20:10.049 --> 01:20:12.039
I don't know. I had this idea...


01:20:12.217 --> 01:20:15.380
...that maybe I could figure something out
and change my life.


01:20:16.088 --> 01:20:17.578
I was wrong.


01:20:17.756 --> 01:20:23.126
Carter. I am 133 years old.


01:20:23.295 --> 01:20:25.661
Oh, Grandma. That's impossible.


01:20:25.831 --> 01:20:30.700
I have spent my life
trying to figure out something.


01:20:30.869 --> 01:20:32.735
And you know what?


01:20:33.405 --> 01:20:35.738
It's not going well.


01:20:37.911 --> 01:20:39.640
I didn't say anything.


01:20:39.812 --> 01:20:44.545
I'll be dead soon and you'll still be alive.


01:20:44.717 --> 01:20:46.844
So stop complaining.


01:20:57.896 --> 01:20:59.261
Hey.


01:21:00.499 --> 01:21:01.989
Where did everyone go?


01:21:02.601 --> 01:21:06.766
Paige was falling asleep.
She wanted to stay...


01:21:07.139 --> 01:21:09.472
...but I just felt like being alone.


01:21:10.976 --> 01:21:12.443
Okay.


01:21:13.679 --> 01:21:15.510
We should talk.


01:21:34.466 --> 01:21:37.264
I'm not really sure
where we go from here.


01:21:38.404 --> 01:21:41.896
Maybe you should start
by telling me why you're mad at me.


01:21:47.212 --> 01:21:49.180
It's hard to even--


01:21:50.148 --> 01:21:51.775
I mean...


01:21:52.517 --> 01:21:54.348
...l've been at it for so long...


01:21:54.519 --> 01:22:00.389
...that I think I'd probably be mad at you
for pretty much everything.


01:22:00.559 --> 01:22:02.255
I mean, anything.


01:22:11.670 --> 01:22:15.572
You know, they did another CAT scan
before the chemo last week.


01:22:16.942 --> 01:22:20.673
They say that apparently the surgery
was very successful.


01:22:21.013 --> 01:22:23.948
There aren't any cancer cells
that they can see...


01:22:24.116 --> 01:22:27.847
...so all this shit that I have to go through
is to make sure.


01:22:31.156 --> 01:22:33.351
But I know I'm gonna be all right.


01:22:34.259 --> 01:22:36.625
And I didn't before.


01:22:38.163 --> 01:22:40.154
I was really afraid.


01:22:48.774 --> 01:22:52.369
I don't wanna miss the part
where I actually get to know you.


01:22:56.748 --> 01:23:02.277
Listen, I don't know what happens next,
either. I don't know.


01:23:04.122 --> 01:23:05.885
I'm just gonna keep loving you.


01:23:06.558 --> 01:23:09.527
And I'm gonna keep hoping
you let me into your life.


01:23:10.128 --> 01:23:12.824
And I will make mistakes, of course...


01:23:13.732 --> 01:23:15.927
...but I will always be there for you.


01:23:21.106 --> 01:23:24.872
There's just one thing
that you've got to do for me.


01:23:25.911 --> 01:23:27.242
What?


01:23:31.917 --> 01:23:33.975
You've got to quit smoking.


01:23:36.320 --> 01:23:37.583
- Okay.
- Okay?


01:23:37.756 --> 01:23:40.247
- I will.
- Okay.


01:23:43.161 --> 01:23:45.424
You should be sleeping, Mom.


01:24:22.200 --> 01:24:23.497
<i>Dear Sarah.</i>


01:24:23.668 --> 01:24:26.159
<i>I've been trying to write this letter
for a while.</i>


01:24:26.338 --> 01:24:28.271
<i>The kind you said you'd never received.</i>


01:24:28.440 --> 01:24:30.907
<i>The kind I've been working on
my whole life.</i>


01:24:31.076 --> 01:24:34.136
<i>I remember being 13 years old,
sitting in my room all night...</i>


01:24:34.312 --> 01:24:36.610
<i>... listening to the same song
over and over.</i>


01:24:37.249 --> 01:24:41.618
<i>I thought that if I could write
something beautiful, something honest...</i>


01:24:41.787 --> 01:24:44.255
<i>... maybe I could make someone love me.</i>


01:24:45.857 --> 01:24:47.620
<i>I've taken a lot for granted.</i>


01:24:48.926 --> 01:24:51.987
<i>I never tried too hard.
I've always avoided responsibility.</i>


01:24:52.430 --> 01:24:55.558
<i>I came here because I was running away.
I wanted to be alone.</i>


01:24:55.733 --> 01:24:57.827
<i>Instead, I met you.</i>


01:24:58.003 --> 01:25:01.403
<i>I met you, and you weren't
taking anything for granted.</i>


01:25:05.410 --> 01:25:07.775
<i>I hope you get
all the moments you deserve.</i>


01:25:08.312 --> 01:25:10.804
<i>I hope you go back to New York
and sit in the Met...</i>


01:25:10.982 --> 01:25:13.815
<i>... in the room with the paintings
of the Hudson River.</i>


01:25:14.752 --> 01:25:18.814
<i>And I hope when you do,
you take Lucy with you...</i>


01:25:19.357 --> 01:25:21.347
<i>... because I know she would love it.</i>


01:25:30.836 --> 01:25:33.702
<i>I'm sorry if I've made your life
more complicated.</i>


01:25:33.871 --> 01:25:36.204
<i>I'm sorry for a lot of things,
but most of all...</i>


01:25:36.374 --> 01:25:41.242
<i>... I'm sorry I never got the chance
to tell you no matter what happens next...</i>


01:25:41.412 --> 01:25:45.850
<i>... I'll never be anything but grateful
for every moment I spent with you.</i>


01:25:46.017 --> 01:25:48.679
<i>And even though I keep fumbling
for the right words...</i>


01:25:48.854 --> 01:25:52.619
<i>... all I really wanted to say
was thank you.</i>


01:26:38.736 --> 01:26:40.328
Grandma.


01:26:41.005 --> 01:26:42.701
Grandma.


01:26:42.874 --> 01:26:45.240
I had one of my children's books
FedEx'd from L.A.


01:26:45.410 --> 01:26:49.846
<i>It's called Pandy: The Unlovable
Self-Destructive Teddy Bear.</i>


01:26:50.481 --> 01:26:51.813
You might really like it.


01:26:51.983 --> 01:26:54.314
There's no pictures yet,
because you'll--


01:26:55.253 --> 01:26:57.777
Grandma? Phyllis.


01:26:57.955 --> 01:27:00.617
Grandma. Wake up.


01:27:02.459 --> 01:27:03.858
Grandma?


01:27:15.073 --> 01:27:18.508
Okay. Yeah.


01:27:29.486 --> 01:27:31.387
Grandma.


01:29:57.401 --> 01:29:59.369
You wrote me a letter.


01:30:06.376 --> 01:30:08.571
It's freezing out here.


01:30:10.414 --> 01:30:15.579
Seriously, I mean, I've heard things,
but this is ridiculous. It's-- You know?


01:30:15.752 --> 01:30:17.845
It's depressing.


01:30:21.558 --> 01:30:23.651
I'm gonna miss you a little bit.


01:30:25.462 --> 01:30:26.656
Good.


01:30:31.701 --> 01:30:34.068
Do you maybe want to go for a walk
or something?


01:30:38.542 --> 01:30:40.908
I can't. I have to--


01:30:41.078 --> 01:30:43.137
I have to get back inside.


01:30:45.849 --> 01:30:47.339
Okay.


01:30:48.051 --> 01:30:49.848
I'll see you around.


01:30:58.628 --> 01:31:00.221
Goodbye, Sarah.


01:31:02.866 --> 01:31:04.299
Wait.


01:31:06.002 --> 01:31:08.335
You know, I have to have the last word.


01:31:10.240 --> 01:31:11.867
You're welcome.


01:31:32.362 --> 01:31:33.727
Stumped?


01:31:35.031 --> 01:31:38.228
Yeah, I guess. I was so close.


01:31:38.402 --> 01:31:40.063
To what?


01:31:40.404 --> 01:31:42.201
Being finished.


01:31:42.372 --> 01:31:44.203
Well, what happened?


01:31:45.809 --> 01:31:48.744
I just feel like it's missing something
at the end.


01:31:49.613 --> 01:31:51.080
You have any ideas for me?


01:31:51.715 --> 01:31:52.909
What's it about?


01:31:53.717 --> 01:31:56.277
My grandmother. She passed away.


01:31:57.354 --> 01:32:00.585
- Sorry. Was she wonderful?
- Yeah. She was pretty wonderful.


01:32:00.757 --> 01:32:03.624
- Did you spend a lot of time with her?
- Towards the end.


01:32:04.761 --> 01:32:06.421
That's nice.


01:32:07.030 --> 01:32:09.793
That's a really nice thing
to be writing about.


01:32:11.768 --> 01:32:13.633
No. I got no ideas.


01:32:13.804 --> 01:32:15.169
That's so disappointing.


01:32:15.338 --> 01:32:18.206
It would have been so cool
if I could have just come in...


01:32:18.375 --> 01:32:21.606
...and given you that perfect nugget
of genius, and then walked away.


01:32:21.777 --> 01:32:23.803
It's what any decent waitress
would've done.


01:32:23.980 --> 01:32:26.313
- Sorry. Settle for a refill?
- Okay.


01:32:28.385 --> 01:32:29.852
I'm Carter.


01:32:30.020 --> 01:32:31.851
Janey. Very nice to meet you.


01:32:32.022 --> 01:32:33.989
Yeah. You too.


01:32:34.156 --> 01:32:36.421
You know, if you're not too busy...


01:32:36.593 --> 01:32:40.620
...I was wondering maybe do you
wanna read the scene I'm working on?


01:32:40.796 --> 01:32:44.130
It's really rough, but I think
I could really use some fresh eyes.


01:32:44.301 --> 01:32:48.670
Okay. But I have to warn you,
I'm a really tough critic.


01:32:48.839 --> 01:32:50.306
Terrific.

